//@version=6
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PRAGYAM  ·  CALIBRATED RISK, EXPOSURE AND SELF-AUDIT                      v2.4
//  "How far can it go, how much should I hold - and has that been true here?"
//
//  Pragyam, from prajñā - discernment: telling what can be known from what
//  cannot. This script forecasts only what the data says can be forecast,
//  states every forecast as a probability, and then tests itself on the chart.
//  (Developed as Kasauti through v2.3; the engine is unchanged.)
//
//  v2.4 · THE PALETTE, BY MEANING. No engine number changed.
//    GREEN / RED   direction, and nothing else. BRIGHT for the short horizon -
//                  the surprise columns and the stretch ladder. DEEP for the
//                  long one - the trend tape. Same meaning, different speed,
//                  so the tape reads as the backdrop the columns move against.
//    GREY          no direction: a flat trend, a move the trend does not back,
//                  a tape still warming.
//    GOLD          risk, and only risk: both risk tapes run from faint to
//                  solid gold. Calm is the absence of gold, not another colour.
//    BLUE          the cone: its learned bands in the pane, the forward cone,
//                  the landing band and the midline on the price chart.
//    COLUMNS       coloured only when the surprise and the trend AGREE - green
//                  up in an uptrend, red down in a downtrend. A move against
//                  the trend, or with no trend behind it, is grey. Solid when
//                  the close left the cone. So a green column never points
//                  down, and colour means "this move has the trend behind it".
//                  Descriptive: no direction was measured in either.
//    MIDLINE       one pixel in the cone's blue, clearer than the landing
//                  band's edges and quieter than the profile's VWAP.
//    STOP LABELS   sit on the stops themselves - the short stop's above its
//                  line over the cone, the long stop's below - out of the
//                  profile's tag column.
//
//  ONE SCRIPT. Everything - the pane, the tapes, the cone and stops, the
//  volume profile and the table - is this one indicator. The only data it
//  requests is the chart symbol's own lower timeframe, for the profile.
//
//  v2.1 · THE VOLUME PROFILE, carried in whole from Pragati (section 7): the
//  session histogram with POC and value area, VWAP, Initial Balance, prior-
//  session levels and naked POCs. Display only - nothing in the risk engine,
//  the cone, the stops, the dial or the ledger reads it. It sits to the right
//  of the forward cone.
//  No engine number changed from v2.0.
//
//  v2.2 · THE MIDLINE, AND ITS RECORD (section 6b). The average of the landing
//  band's two edges, drawn on the price chart. The observation it came from:
//  while price is below it price tends to go lower until it gets back above,
//  and the strongest runs start when risk is calm and the trend or the
//  histogram flips. MEASURED on 151 instruments, 2001-2026 (research/
//  midline.txt), it did not hold as a forward signal:
//    · the next bar's return per unit of risk was the same above the midline
//      and below it (2.80 against 2.88, σ × 100), in every era, in every risk
//      regime and on either side of the trend tape;
//    · after a close across it, the next 10 bars were no different from any
//      other 10 bars - including crosses made in calm risk, and crosses that
//      came with a trend flip;
//    · held as a rule - long above, flat below - it made a Sharpe of 0.24
//      against 0.48 for buy and hold; long / short lost money; on hourly bars
//      every version lost.
//  WHY IT LOOKS TRUE ON A CHART. A run below the midline lasts a long time
//  only if price kept falling. Those long runs - one in eleven lasts 20 bars
//  or more, and they average 7 to 10% - are what the eye finds. The other ten
//  are over in a few bars (the median run is 4), and only 37% of all runs end
//  in profit. The midline is the surprise histogram's zero line, drawn on
//  price: it says where price stands against 10 bars ago. It is a description.
//  So it is drawn as a LINE, with this chart's own record of it in the table,
//  and its crossings are optional marks - not a signal.
//
//  WHY IT IS NOT A DIRECTION ORACLE. Measured first (research/, 151 instruments
//  in seven classes, daily bars 2001-2026, three eras): no price or volume
//  state tried - trend, stretch, dips, volume, overnight against session,
//  efficiency - led the next 10 bars in a way that held in all three eras.
//  What IS forecastable is RISK: the next 10 bars' variance is predicted out
//  of sample with a log R² of 0.71. So this script forecasts risk and turns it
//  into the three numbers a position needs: how far, how much, where it is
//  wrong.
//
//  v2.3 · PRESENTATION CLOSED, TWO MORE OBSERVATIONS TESTED. No engine number
//  changed.
//    STATUS LINE   carries the surprise and nothing else: no input values, no
//                  tape or band readings.
//    PRICE CHART   the MIDLINE is the one prominent line; the landing band's
//                  two edges are drawn faint behind it. The profile's
//                  developing trails are off by default, and Initial Balance is
//                  drawn on intraday charts only - on a daily chart its twelve
//                  bars outlast the session.
//    COLUMNS       (recoloured again in v2.4 - see above.)
//    TABLE         eight short rows, off by default. Each row's detail is in
//                  its tooltip.
//    TESTED (research/observations.txt, 151 instruments):
//      · "The stop that is further from the close tells the trend." It does
//        not: the long stop is the further one on 39% of bars in downtrends,
//        in flat markets and in uptrends alike, and what followed was the same
//        either way (next 10 bars 7.4 against 7.7, σ × 100).
//      · "VWAP, with the midline and the stops." Closes BELOW the session VWAP
//        were followed by the higher next-bar return (4.5 against 1.3 on daily
//        bars, 1.6 against −0.2 on hourly) - a one-bar reversal, the opposite
//        of a trend reading - and it is gone a bar later and after costs. All
//        three agreeing was followed by nothing consistent across eras, and
//        every rule built from them lost to buy and hold.
//
//  ═══ WHAT IS ON THE PANE, TOP TO BOTTOM ═══════════════════════════════════
//      +5.15 STRETCH LADDER    thin · how many horizons closed outside
//      +4.3  TREND             the move over a quarter, a half, a year - in σ
//      +q    landing band      the learned upper edge
//        0   SURPRISE          the realised H-bar move ÷ the forecast made H
//                              bars ago; solid when the close left the band
//      −q    landing band      the learned lower edge
//      −4.3  RISK              calm · normal · stressed
//      −5.15 RISK MOMENTUM     thin · risk rising · steady · falling
//  Columns and band are clipped at ±3.5 for display; the status line carries
//  the unclipped surprise.
//
//  ON THE PRICE CHART: the CONE forward from the last bar, the long and short
//  STOPS across it, the LANDING band - the cone drawn H bars ago, at today's
//  bar - the VOLUME PROFILE to the cone's right, and the table.
//
//  ═══ THE TAPES · WHAT EACH ONE CHANGES ════════════════════════════════════
//  A tape is here only if a number depends on it. The two inner tapes are the
//  two things the cone and the dial LISTEN to; the two outer tapes say where
//  each is heading.
//
//  TREND          green up, red down, in the deep tone; faint while flat.
//      · It SKEWS THE CONE. Before the cone listened to it, a short stop in a
//        downtrend was touched 27% of the time against a stated 20%, and a
//        long stop in an uptrend 22%. With it: 21% and 20%.
//      · It is the dial's THROTTLE and the ledger's row.
//  STRETCH LADDER   the surprise at four horizons - H/2, H, 2H, 4H -
//      each against its OWN learned cone. Hue: the side. Intensity: how many
//      rungs are outside - faint none, clear one or two, solid three or four.
//      · Three or four rungs outside happens on about 4% of bars a side.
//      · It carries NO direction (measured, all three eras).
//      · After a ladder-wide break BELOW, a long stop is touched about a
//        quarter of the time, not a fifth - the one place the stops still
//        understate. The table's LONG STOP row turns gold there.
//  RISK           gold only, faint while calm to solid when stressed - where forecast risk
//      stands among its last 500 bars.
//      · It sets the cone's WIDTH term and the dial's first factor.
//      · Stressed risk fell over the next 10 bars (median −8%); calm risk did
//        not rise (+1%). Stress fades; calm persists.
//  RISK MOMENTUM  gold while rising, grey while falling, faint steady - the change
//      in forecast risk over the last H bars, past ±10%.
//      · RISING is a spike, and spikes fade: risk was LOWER 10 bars later 74%
//        of the time (median −11%), in every era. A cone drawn into a spike
//        is at its widest.
//
//  GOLD, everywhere here, means risk - never up or down. Blue is the cone.
//
//  ═══ HOW IT WORKS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//    RISK      per-bar variance from the bar's whole range and its gap
//              (Garman-Klass), blended over three horizons - 0.25 · 5-bar +
//              0.40 · 22-bar + 0.35 · 252-bar - and rescaled to close-to-close.
//              Beats a 20-bar standard deviation by 30% (QLIKE) out of sample.
//    CONE      close · exp(± q · σ · √H). q is not a normal quantile: it is
//              LEARNED. Every bar the forecast made H bars ago is settled; a
//              miss widens q, a hit narrows it, in the ratio that makes the
//              miss rate converge on the target (adaptive conformal
//              inference). log q = a term for the risk regime + a term for
//              the trend state, each side separately - so fat tails and skew
//              are measured, not assumed.
//    STOPS     the same, settled on the lowest low (highest high) of the H
//              bars instead of the last close.
//    EXPOSURE  the instrument's own average risk ÷ risk now, capped, times a
//              trend throttle between a floor and 1. Changed only in steps.
//    LEDGER    nine states - trend down / flat / up × the surprise below /
//              inside / above the cone. For each, the next H bars' return in
//              σ, against this chart's own mean, shrunk toward "no edge". A
//              state is called PROVEN only past two posterior σ.
//
//  ═══ MEASURED (research/results.txt · the Python port is research/pragyam.py)
//    CALIBRATION   cone 80%: realised 80.0%; within 3 points of target in 99%
//                  of instrument-eras (a fixed normal band: 61%). Stops 20%:
//                  realised 20.0%, within 3 points in 99%. A 2 × ATR(14) stop
//                  is touched anywhere from 17% to 44% of the time depending
//                  on the instrument. Holds at H 5, 20 and 40, at 50% and 90%
//                  cones, on weekly bars and on hourly bars.
//    EXPOSURE      daily: Sharpe 0.55 against 0.53 for buy and hold, mean worst
//                  drawdown −44% against −62%, shallower on 99% of instruments
//                  or more in every era. After 2013 it does NOT beat buy and
//                  hold on Sharpe: it is risk control, not a return engine.
//                  Weekly: the same shape. HOURLY: IT LOST (0.26 against 0.42)
//                  - the dial is a daily and weekly tool.
//    LEDGER        pooled, no state reaches |t| = 1.3 outside crypto. On a daily
//                  chart almost every state will read UNPROVEN. That is the
//                  finding, not a fault.
//
//  WHAT IT WILL NOT DO. It does not call direction. The cone is a range, not
//  a target. Calibration is a long-run frequency: a cone can miss several
//  times in a row inside one shock. Stocks in the study are today's large
//  caps, which flatters buy and hold and the dial alike.
//
//  REPAINT POSTURE. The risk engine, cone, stops, tapes, dial and ledger are
//  computed from the chart's own bars. Values on the forming bar move until it
//  closes; history and realtime compute the same numbers. Alerts fire on closed
//  bars. The volume profile's developing session is the one disclosed
//  exception, as in Pragati.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("Pragyam · Calibrated Risk, Exposure and Self-Audit", shorttitle = "Pragyam", overlay = false,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 100, max_boxes_count = 500, max_polylines_count = 5)

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  INPUTS
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_D = "1 · Display"
var string G_F = "2 · Forecast"
var string G_E = "3 · Exposure"
var string G_A = "4 · Advanced"

// Tooltips: first line says what it does; "Measured:" gives one number.
string inpPane  = input.string("Surprise", "Pane", options = ["Surprise", "Proof"], group = G_D, tooltip = "Surprise: the 10-bar move divided by its forecast, against the landing band, with the tapes.\n\nProof: growth of following exposure against buy and hold on this chart, one bar late, net of costs.", display = display.none)
bool   inpTapes = input.bool(true, "Tapes", group = G_D, tooltip = "Trend and risk next to the columns - what the cone and exposure read. Stretch ladder and risk momentum, thinner, outside them - context.", display = display.none)
bool   inpCone  = input.bool(true, "Forward cone", group = G_D, tooltip = "Where the close should be one horizon from now, with the long and short stops across it.", display = display.none)
bool   inpLand  = input.bool(true, "Landing band", group = G_D, tooltip = "The cone drawn one horizon ago, at today's bar. A close outside it is a miss.", display = display.none)
bool   inpMid   = input.bool(true, "Midline", group = G_D, tooltip = "The middle of the landing band, close to where price stood one horizon ago.\n\nNot a signal. Measured: long above, flat below made a Sharpe of 0.24 against 0.48 for buy and hold.", display = display.none)
bool   inpMidMk = input.bool(false, "    Cross marks", group = G_D, tooltip = "A dot on each bar that closes across the midline.\n\nMeasured: 37% of the runs that follow end in profit.", display = display.none)
bool   inpTrail = input.bool(false, "Stop history", group = G_D, tooltip = "Where the long and short stops stood on every past bar.", display = display.none)
bool   inpTbl   = input.bool(false, "Table", group = G_D, tooltip = "Eight short rows on the price chart: cone, stops and size, exposure, this chart's record, risk, trend, Sharpe against buy and hold.", display = display.none)
string inpPos   = input.string("Bottom left", "    Corner", options = ["Bottom left", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Top right"], group = G_D, tooltip = "Bottom left is clear of the volume profile.", display = display.none)
bool   inpMark  = input.bool(true, "Proven-state marks", group = G_D, tooltip = "A faint triangle where the chart enters a state its own history has proven. Rare.\n\nMeasured: pooled across 151 instruments no state had a reliable edge.", display = display.none)
string inpTheme = input.string("Auto", "Theme", options = ["Auto", "Light", "Dark"], group = G_D, tooltip = "Auto follows the chart background.", display = display.none)

int    inpH     = input.int(10, "Horizon (bars)", minval = 4, maxval = 60, group = G_F, tooltip = "How far ahead every forecast looks: the cone, the stops' touch probability, the stretch ladder (half, one, two and four horizons).\n\nMeasured at 5, 10, 20 and 40 bars: cone and stops held their targets.", display = display.none)
float  inpCover = input.float(80.0, "Cone coverage (%)", minval = 50.0, maxval = 98.0, step = 5.0, group = G_F, tooltip = "How often the close one horizon ahead should land inside the cone. The cone learns its width until this is true on this chart.\n\nMeasured: realised within 3 points of target on 99% of instrument-eras.", display = display.none)
float  inpStop  = input.float(20.0, "Stop touch probability (%)", minval = 5.0, maxval = 50.0, step = 5.0, group = G_F, tooltip = "How often price should trade at the stop within one horizon. A tighter stop is touched more often.\n\nMeasured: realised 20.0% at a 20% target.", display = display.none)
float  inpRisk  = input.float(1.0, "Risk per trade (%)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = G_F, tooltip = "Share of equity lost if the stop is touched. Sets the size shown beside each stop in the table.", display = display.none)

string inpMode  = input.string("Risk × trend", "Exposure rule", options = ["Risk × trend", "Risk only"], group = G_E, tooltip = "How much of a full position to carry. Daily and weekly charts only: on hourly bars it lost to buy and hold.\n\nRisk only: usual risk ÷ risk now. Risk × trend: the same, cut in a downtrend. Measured: worst drawdown about a quarter shallower, Sharpe level.", display = display.none)
float  inpCap   = input.float(1.0, "    Max exposure", minval = 0.25, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.25, group = G_E, tooltip = "The most exposure may read. 1.0 never levers.\n\nMeasured at 1.5 and 2.0: more return, and the drawdown advantage is gone.", display = display.none)

float  inpEta   = input.float(0.02, "Learning speed", minval = 0.005, maxval = 0.10, step = 0.005, group = G_A, tooltip = "How far one settled forecast moves a learned width. Higher holds the target more tightly with a wider, jumpier cone.\n\nMeasured: 0.02 gave the narrowest cone that still held its target.", display = display.none)
bool   inpReg   = input.bool(true, "Adapt cone to risk", group = G_A, tooltip = "A separate learned width for calm, normal and stressed markets.\n\nMeasured: without it the cone held 76% in calm markets and 84% in stressed ones, against a target of 80%.", display = display.none)
bool   inpTrF   = input.bool(true, "Adapt cone to trend", group = G_A, tooltip = "A learned term for downtrend, flat and uptrend, each side separately.\n\nMeasured: without it a short stop in a downtrend was touched 27% of the time, against a target of 20%.", display = display.none)
float  inpFloor = input.float(0.5, "Trend floor", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.25, group = G_A, tooltip = "The least a downtrend may cut exposure to. 0.5 halves it, never closes it.\n\nMeasured: lower floors gave shallower drawdowns and lost Sharpe on most instruments.", display = display.none)
float  inpStep  = input.float(0.10, "Exposure step", minval = 0.0, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.05, group = G_A, tooltip = "Exposure changes only when it has moved this far.\n\nMeasured: 0.10 cut turnover by about two thirds at no cost to Sharpe or drawdown.", display = display.none)
float  inpCost  = input.float(5.0, "Proof cost (bp)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 1.0, group = G_A, tooltip = "Charged in the proof on every change of exposure, per unit of change. The study used 5, and 10 for crypto.", display = display.none)
float  inpTau   = input.float(0.10, "Believable edge (σ)", minval = 0.02, maxval = 0.50, step = 0.01, group = G_A, tooltip = "The ledger assumes a state has no edge, and that a real one is about this large. Evidence must overcome that before a state reads proven.\n\nMeasured: on random walks it calls a state proven on 0.4% of bars.", display = display.none)

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  PALETTE
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
float bgLum    = color.r(chart.bg_color) * 0.299 + color.g(chart.bg_color) * 0.587 + color.b(chart.bg_color) * 0.114
bool  darkMode = inpTheme == "Dark" or (inpTheme == "Auto" and bgLum < 128)
color C_UP    = darkMode ? #3FB980 : #08724A
color C_DN    = darkMode ? #E4776A : #A8443A
color C_UPD   = darkMode ? #2A8660 : #5C9E86               // the same direction on the long horizon: deep, for the trend tape
color C_DND   = darkMode ? #B4554B : #BC7A72
color C_NEUT  = darkMode ? #8A97A0 : #69757E
color C_CONE  = darkMode ? #5B8FD6 : #2C5C99
color C_GOLD  = darkMode ? #D9B44A : #8A6A0E               // risk - never a direction
color C_TEXT  = darkMode ? #C9D1D6 : #2B3338
color C_PANEL = darkMode ? color.new(#0D1215, 8) : color.new(#FFFFFF, 6)

// profile palette — PVOI's, as in Pragati
color C_POC    = darkMode ? #FFB020 : #B26A00      // point of control — warm anchor
color C_VA     = darkMode ? #5B8FD6 : #2C5C99      // value-area boundaries + band, cool
color C_VWAP   = darkMode ? #F06BA8 : #A32468      // volume-weighted average, rose
color C_NODE   = darkMode ? #6E7C88 : #8A949B      // monochrome out-of-value tails · neutral grey
color C_HVN    = darkMode ? #8F7BD8 : #5E4B9E      // High-Volume Node · dense violet
color C_LVN    = darkMode ? #C6BBEA : #8F7DBB      // Low-Volume Node  · pale  violet
color C_VIOLET = darkMode ? #A87ABF : #6A3F84      // Initial Balance

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  HELPERS
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_tanh(float x) =>
    float xc = math.max(-10.0, math.min(10.0, x))
    float e  = math.exp(2.0 * xc)
    (e - 1.0) / (e + 1.0)

// Inverse normal CDF (Acklam), accurate to 2e-9. Used once, to start the
// learned widths where a normal distribution would put them.
f_invTail(float q) =>
    (((((-7.784894002430293e-03 * q - 3.223964580411365e-01) * q - 2.400758277161838) * q - 2.549732539343734) * q + 4.374664141464968) * q + 2.938163982698783) /
     ((((7.784695709041462e-03 * q + 3.224671290700398e-01) * q + 2.445134137142996) * q + 3.754408661907416) * q + 1.0)
f_invNorm(float p) =>
    float x = 0.0
    if p < 0.02425
        x := f_invTail(math.sqrt(-2.0 * math.log(p)))
    else if p > 1.0 - 0.02425
        x := -f_invTail(math.sqrt(-2.0 * math.log(1.0 - p)))
    else
        float q = p - 0.5
        float r = q * q
        x := (((((-3.969683028665376e+01 * r + 2.209460984245205e+02) * r - 2.759285104469687e+02) * r + 1.383577518672690e+02) * r - 3.066479806614716e+01) * r + 2.506628277459239) * q /
             (((((-5.447609879822406e+01 * r + 1.615858368580409e+02) * r - 1.556989798598866e+02) * r + 6.680131188771972e+01) * r - 1.328068155288572e+01) * r + 1.0)
    x

f_pct(float x, string fmt) => na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(100.0 * x, fmt) + "%"
f_num(float x, string fmt) => na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(x, fmt)
f_px(float x)              => na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(x, format.mintick)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  1 · THE RISK FORECAST
//
//  One bar's variance from its whole range and its gap (Garman-Klass), which
//  uses about five times the information of a squared close-to-close return.
//  Three horizons blended with fixed weights, then rescaled so the level
//  matches close-to-close variance on this instrument. The weights are round
//  numbers near a fit on 2001-2012 and beat that fit on 2013-2026.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
const int WARM = 252
const int RN   = 500

float lc = math.log(close)
float lnO = math.log(open)
float r1 = lc - lc[1]
float gp = lnO - lc[1]
float co = lc - lnO
float hl = math.log(high) - math.log(low)
float gk = gp * gp + 0.5 * hl * hl - (2.0 * math.log(2.0) - 1.0) * co * co
float vBar  = hl > 0.0 and gk > 0.0 ? gk : r1 * r1            // a bar with no range falls back to its squared return
float varS = ta.ema(vBar, 5)
float varM = ta.ema(vBar, 22)
float varL = ta.ema(vBar, 252)
float rL = ta.ema(r1 * r1, 252)
float kk = varL > 0.0 ? math.max(0.5, math.min(2.0, rL / varL)) : 1.0
float s0 = bar_index >= WARM ? math.sqrt(kk * (0.25 * varS + 0.40 * varM + 0.35 * varL)) : na
float sig = s0 > 0.0 ? s0 : na                              // risk per bar, in log return
float sH  = sig * math.sqrt(inpH)                           // risk over the horizon

// THE RISK TAPE: where this bar's risk stands among the last RN bars.
float prk    = ta.percentrank(sig, RN)
bool  regOk  = bar_index >= WARM + RN and not na(prk)
int   regRaw = regOk ? (prk < 100.0 / 3.0 ? 0 : prk < 200.0 / 3.0 ? 1 : 2) : 1
int   reg    = inpReg ? regRaw : 1                          // the regime the cone listens to

// RISK MOMENTUM: the change in forecast risk over the last H bars.
float rMom = math.log(sig / sig[inpH])
int   rmS  = rMom > 0.10 ? 2 : rMom < -0.10 ? 0 : 1

// THE TREND TAPE, in σ: the move over a quarter, a half and a whole year of
// bars, each divided by what today's risk says such a move should be.
float T = ((lc - lc[63]) / (sig * math.sqrt(63.0)) + (lc - lc[126]) / (sig * math.sqrt(126.0)) + (lc - lc[252]) / (sig * math.sqrt(252.0))) / 3.0
int trRaw = T > 0.5 ? 2 : T < -0.5 ? 0 : 1
int trs   = inpTrF ? trRaw : 1                              // the trend state the cone listens to

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  2 · THE CONE, THE STOPS AND THE LADDER · LEARNED WIDTHS
//
//  Each bar settles the forecast made h bars ago: where the close landed, in
//  units of that forecast's own σ. Each width then moves in logs by
//
//      log q ← log q + η · ( miss − target )
//
//  so it rises on a miss and falls on a hit in exactly the ratio at which the
//  miss rate equals the target. log q is the sum of a term for the risk regime
//  and a term for the trend state the forecast was made in, and both terms
//  take the step - so the target is met in every regime and in every trend
//  state, with six numbers a side instead of nine. No distribution is assumed.
//
//  A width array holds six numbers: [0..2] by risk regime, [3..5] by trend.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float aTail = (1.0 - inpCover / 100.0) / 2.0
float pTch  = inpStop / 100.0
float zInit = math.log(f_invNorm(1.0 - aTail))
float sInit = math.log(f_invNorm(1.0 - pTch / 2.0))         // a Brownian path touches −b with probability 2·Φ(−b)

f_new(float b0) =>
    array<float> a = array.new_float(6, 0.0)
    array.set(a, 0, b0)
    array.set(a, 1, b0)
    array.set(a, 2, b0)
    a
f_q(array<float> a, int rg, int tr) => math.exp(array.get(a, rg) + array.get(a, 3 + tr))
f_step(array<float> a, int rg, int tr, float e) =>
    array.set(a, rg, array.get(a, rg) + e)
    array.set(a, 3 + tr, array.get(a, 3 + tr) + (inpTrF ? e : 0.0))

// One rung of the horizon ladder. Returns the surprise, the band it is judged
// against (the one in force when its forecast was made), whether it broke
// either side, whether it has settled, the surprise as a fraction of its band,
// and the widths now in force.
f_rung(simple int h, array<float> wU, array<float> wD) =>
    float qu  = na
    float qd  = na
    float uu  = (lc - lc[h]) / (sig[h] * math.sqrt(h))
    float quP = qu[h]
    float qdP = qd[h]
    int   rgP = reg[h]
    int   trP = trs[h]
    bool  ok  = not na(uu) and not na(quP)
    bool  up  = ok and uu >  quP
    bool  dn  = ok and uu < -qdP
    if ok
        f_step(wU, rgP, trP, inpEta * ((up ? 1.0 : 0.0) - aTail))
        f_step(wD, rgP, trP, inpEta * ((dn ? 1.0 : 0.0) - aTail))
    if not na(sig)
        qu := f_q(wU, reg, trs)
        qd := f_q(wD, reg, trs)
    float x = not ok ? na : uu >= 0.0 ? uu / quP : uu / qdP
    [uu, quP, qdP, up, dn, ok, x, qu, qd]

int h0 = math.max(2, int(math.floor(inpH / 2)))
int h2 = 2 * inpH
int h3 = 4 * inpH

var array<float> wU0 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD0 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wU1 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD1 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wU2 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD2 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wU3 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD3 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wS  = f_new(sInit)                         // long stop
var array<float> wR  = f_new(sInit)                         // short stop

[u0, bU0, bD0, up0, dn0, ok0, lx0, qU0, qD0] = f_rung(h0,   wU0, wD0)
[u,  bU,  bD,  mU,  mD,  settled, lx1, qU, qD] = f_rung(inpH, wU1, wD1)     // the pane's own rung
[u2, bU2, bD2, up2, dn2, ok2, lx2, qU2, qD2] = f_rung(h2,   wU2, wD2)
[u3, bU3, bD3, up3, dn3, ok3, lx3, qU3, qD3] = f_rung(h3,   wU3, wD3)

// THE STRETCH LADDER: how many rungs are outside their own cone, and its mean
// position as a fraction of the bands.
bool  ladOk  = ok0 and settled and ok2 and ok3
int   ladUp  = (up0 ? 1 : 0) + (mU ? 1 : 0) + (up2 ? 1 : 0) + (up3 ? 1 : 0)
int   ladDn  = (dn0 ? 1 : 0) + (mD ? 1 : 0) + (dn2 ? 1 : 0) + (dn3 ? 1 : 0)
float ladX   = ladOk ? (lx0 + lx1 + lx2 + lx3) / 4.0 : na
int   ladN   = ladX >= 0.0 ? ladUp : ladDn                  // rungs outside on the side it leans

// The stops: settled on the path, not the close.
float qS = na
float qR = na
float pS = (math.log(ta.lowest(low, inpH))   - lc[inpH]) / sH[inpH]
float pR = (math.log(ta.highest(high, inpH)) - lc[inpH]) / sH[inpH]
float qSP = qS[inpH]
float qRP = qR[inpH]
int   regPrev = reg[inpH]
int   trPrev  = trs[inpH]
bool  mS = settled and pS < -qSP                            // the long stop was touched
bool  mR = settled and pR >  qRP                            // the short stop was touched

var int nF  = 0
var int nMU = 0
var int nMD = 0
var int nMS = 0
var int nMR = 0

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  3 · THE LEDGER
//
//  Nine states. For each, every bar spent in it is scored H bars later by the
//  return from the NEXT bar's open to that close, in the forecast's σ, clipped
//  at ±6 so one bad print cannot own a state. Samples are counted as
//  independent only when their signal bars are at least H apart.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var array<float> lCnt  = array.new_float(9, 0.0)
var array<float> lMean = array.new_float(9, 0.0)
var array<float> lEff  = array.new_float(9, 0.0)
var array<int>   lLast = array.new_int(9, -1000000000)
var int   gN = 0
var float gM = 0.0
var float gQ = 0.0

int   st     = -1
float yRaw   = (lc - lnO[inpH - 1]) / sH[inpH]
float yOut      = na(yRaw) ? na : math.max(-6.0, math.min(6.0, yRaw))
int   stPrev = st[inpH]

if settled
    f_step(wS, regPrev, trPrev, inpEta * ((mS ? 1.0 : 0.0) - pTch))
    f_step(wR, regPrev, trPrev, inpEta * ((mR ? 1.0 : 0.0) - pTch))
    nF  += 1
    nMU += mU ? 1 : 0
    nMD += mD ? 1 : 0
    nMS += mS ? 1 : 0
    nMR += mR ? 1 : 0
    if stPrev >= 0 and not na(yOut)
        float c1 = array.get(lCnt, stPrev) + 1.0
        array.set(lCnt, stPrev, c1)
        array.set(lMean, stPrev, array.get(lMean, stPrev) + (yOut - array.get(lMean, stPrev)) / c1)
        gN += 1
        if bar_index - inpH - array.get(lLast, stPrev) >= inpH
            array.set(lEff, stPrev, array.get(lEff, stPrev) + 1.0)
            array.set(lLast, stPrev, bar_index - inpH)
        float dlt = yOut - gM
        gM += dlt / gN
        gQ += dlt * (yOut - gM)

if not na(sig)
    qS := f_q(wS, reg, trs)
    qR := f_q(wR, reg, trs)

int cnS = mU ? 2 : mD ? 0 : 1
if settled and not na(T)
    st := 3 * trRaw + cnS

// This state's record so far, against the chart's own mean, shrunk toward zero.
float lEdge = na
float lPost = na
float lZ    = na
float lNe   = st >= 0 ? array.get(lEff, st) : na
float lMu   = st >= 0 ? array.get(lMean, st) : na
if st >= 0 and lNe >= 5.0 and gN > 30 * inpH
    float se2 = gQ / (gN - 1) / lNe
    float shr = inpTau * inpTau / (inpTau * inpTau + se2)
    lEdge := lMu - gM
    lPost := shr * lEdge
    lZ    := lEdge * math.sqrt(shr / se2)
int  proven   = lZ >= 2.0 ? 1 : lZ <= -2.0 ? -1 : 0
bool stEnter  = st >= 0 and st != st[1]
bool provenUp = barstate.isconfirmed and stEnter and proven ==  1
bool provenDn = barstate.isconfirmed and stEnter and proven == -1

// Calibration over the last 250 settled forecasts - the recent record.
float covRecent = 1.0 - ta.sma(settled ? (mU or mD ? 1.0 : 0.0) : na, 250)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  4 · LEVELS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float upper = close * math.exp( qU * sH)
float lower = close * math.exp(-qD * sH)
float stopL = close * math.exp(-qS * sH)
float stopS = close * math.exp( qR * sH)
bool  coneOk = not na(sig) and not na(qU) and not na(qS)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  5 · THE EXPOSURE DIAL
//
//  The instrument's own average risk so far, over its risk now: one when the
//  instrument is as wild as it usually is, less when it is wilder. The trend
//  throttle runs from the floor in a full downtrend to 1 in a full uptrend.
//  The position HELD follows the dial only in steps.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float sumSig = 0.0
var int   nSig   = 0
if not na(sig)
    sumSig += sig
    nSig   += 1
float sigStar = nSig > 0 ? sumSig / nSig : na
float dialR   = na(sig) ? na : math.min(inpCap, sigStar / sig)
float dialT   = inpMode == "Risk only" ? 1.0 : na(T) ? na : inpFloor + (1.0 - inpFloor) * (0.5 + 0.5 * f_tanh(T))
float dial    = na(T) ? na : dialR * dialT

var float held = na
if not na(dial) and (na(held) or math.abs(dial - held) >= inpStep)
    held := dial
float E = na(dial) ? na : held

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  6 · THE PROOF
//
//  The position held at the close of bar t−2 is the position over bar t: one
//  full bar to act on it. Costs are charged on every change. Buy and hold is
//  scored over the same bars.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float ret = close / close[1] - 1.0
float e2  = E[2]
float e3  = E[3]
float pF  = na(e2) ? na : e2 * ret - inpCost / 10000.0 * math.abs(e2 - nz(e3, 0.0))
float pH  = na(e2) ? na : ret

var int   nP   = 0
var int   tP   = na
var float sF   = 0.0
var float sF2  = 0.0
var float sHd  = 0.0
var float sHd2 = 0.0
var float eqF  = 1.0
var float eqH  = 1.0
var float pkF  = 1.0
var float pkH  = 1.0
var float ddF  = 0.0
var float ddH  = 0.0
if not na(pF) and not na(pH)
    if na(tP)
        tP := time
    nP   += 1
    sF   += pF
    sF2  += pF * pF
    sHd  += pH
    sHd2 += pH * pH
    eqF  *= 1.0 + pF
    eqH  *= 1.0 + pH
    pkF  := math.max(pkF, eqF)
    pkH  := math.max(pkH, eqH)
    ddF  := math.min(ddF, eqF / pkF - 1.0)
    ddH  := math.min(ddH, eqH / pkH - 1.0)

float yrs   = na(tP) ? na : (time - tP) / 31557600000.0
float bpy   = yrs > 0.0 ? nP / yrs : na                     // bars per year, measured on this chart
float sdF   = nP > 1 ? math.sqrt(math.max(sF2 / nP - math.pow(sF / nP, 2), 0.0)) : na
float sdHd  = nP > 1 ? math.sqrt(math.max(sHd2 / nP - math.pow(sHd / nP, 2), 0.0)) : na
float shF   = sdF  > 0.0 ? sF  / nP / sdF  * math.sqrt(bpy) : na
float shH   = sdHd > 0.0 ? sHd / nP / sdHd * math.sqrt(bpy) : na
float cagF  = yrs > 0.0 and eqF > 0.0 ? math.pow(eqF, 1.0 / yrs) - 1.0 : na
float cagH  = yrs > 0.0 and eqH > 0.0 ? math.pow(eqH, 1.0 / yrs) - 1.0 : na

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  6b · THE MIDLINE AND ITS RECORD                         (display and audit)
//
//  The average of the landing band's edges. Nothing reads it. Two records are
//  kept so the observation can be tested on this chart:
//    RUNS   every stretch from one close across the midline to the next, and
//           what price did over it in the run's own direction;
//    RULE   long above, flat below - scored exactly as the dial is: the side
//           at the close of bar t−2 is the position over bar t, net of cost.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float midL    = (upper[inpH] + lower[inpH]) / 2.0
int   midSide = na(midL) ? 0 : close > midL ? 1 : -1
bool  midUp   = midSide == 1 and midSide[1] == -1
bool  midDn   = midSide == -1 and midSide[1] == 1

var int   mRuns = 0
var int   mWon  = 0
var int   mLong = 0
var float mGain = 0.0
var float mPx   = na
var int   mBar  = na
var int   mDir  = 0
if midUp or midDn
    if mDir != 0 and not na(mPx)
        float gRun = mDir * math.log(close / mPx)
        mRuns += 1
        mWon  += gRun > 0.0 ? 1 : 0
        mLong += bar_index - mBar >= 20 ? 1 : 0
        mGain += gRun
    mPx  := close
    mBar := bar_index
    mDir := midUp ? 1 : -1

float m2 = midSide[2] == 1 ? 1.0 : 0.0
float m3 = midSide[3] == 1 ? 1.0 : 0.0
float pM = na(e2) ? na : m2 * ret - inpCost / 10000.0 * math.abs(m2 - m3)
var float sM  = 0.0
var float sM2 = 0.0
if not na(pM) and not na(pH)
    sM  += pM
    sM2 += pM * pM
float sdM = nP > 1 ? math.sqrt(math.max(sM2 / nP - math.pow(sM / nP, 2), 0.0)) : na
float shM = sdM > 0.0 ? sM / nP / sdM * math.sqrt(bpy) : na

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  7 · VOLUME PROFILE · MARKET-STRUCTURE OVERLAY       (Pragati's, from PVOI v2.1)
//  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A PRICE-CHART overlay: session volume profile (histogram + POC/VAH/VAL value
//  area), plus session VWAP, Initial Balance, naked POCs, HVN/LVN nodes,
//  prior-session levels and developing-level trails. Pragyam is a pane script,
//  so every element is drawn with force_overlay = true.
//
//  DISPLAY-ONLY AND FULLY DETACHED. It touches NOTHING - not the risk forecast,
//  the cone, the stops, the dial or the ledger. Everything is namespaced
//  vp*/C_* so it cannot collide with the engine's own state. Removing this
//  whole block leaves Pragyam intact.
//
//  CARRIED IN from Pragati - the build, the value-area walk, the ledger of
//  naked POCs and the render are its own, line for line. What changed is its
//  WEIGHT and its defaults, because here it is context beside a measured cone:
//    · it sits to the RIGHT of the forward cone, 14 bars wide, and its level
//      lines stop at the last bar instead of running through the cone;
//    · rows, POC and value area are drawn fainter than the cone and stops;
//    · trails, node marks and prior-session levels default off, naked POCs
//      keep three, Initial Balance is intraday only;
//    · tags need more room between them before two are seated;
//    · the gates read this script's switches; green / red are C_UP / C_DN.
//  The tag column is the profile's alone: the stops label themselves.
//
//  Sorted-key bins, O(1) POC, value-area walk outward from the POC, optional
//  intrabar distribution and inferred buy/sell delta. Session anchor = D intraday,
//  W on daily, M above. request.security_lower_tf history depth is plan-dependent;
//  the profile falls back to a uniform bar-range spread when it is unavailable.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var string G_VP = "5 · Volume profile"
bool   inpVpMaster    = input.bool(true,  "Volume profile", group=G_VP, tooltip="Draws the session volume profile and its levels on the price chart. Off also stops it being computed.\n\nThe cone, stops and exposure never read it.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpIntrabar  = input.bool(true,  "    Use intrabar data", group=G_VP, tooltip="request.security_lower_tf() distributes volume by ACTUAL traded price. More accurate, slower, plan-dependent history. Falls back automatically.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpUseVol    = input.bool(true,  "    Volume-weighted", group=G_VP, tooltip="Off degrades the profile to a time-at-price (TPO) distribution — for spot FX / synthetic volume.", display=display.none)
string inpVpBinMode   = input.string("ATR adaptive", "    Row size", options=["ATR adaptive", "Fixed ticks"], group=G_VP, display=display.none)
float  inpVpBinsPerAtr= input.float(4.0,  "        Rows per ATR", minval=1.0, maxval=20.0, step=0.5, group=G_VP, tooltip="Bin width = ATR / this. Frozen at session start so keys stay consistent within a profile.", display=display.none)
int    inpVpBinTicks  = input.int(20,     "        Row size (ticks)", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_VP, display=display.none)
float  inpVpVaPct     = input.float(0.70, "    Value area fraction", minval=0.50, maxval=0.95, step=0.01, group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpHistg     = input.bool(true,  "    Histogram", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
string inpVpStyle     = input.string("Monochrome", "        Style", options=["Monochrome", "Delta split"], group=G_VP, tooltip="MONOCHROME (default): one box per row, amber POC row inside blue value-area rows, grey out-of-value tails. Hue marks identity only, never direction.\n\nDELTA SPLIT: each row divides into green (inferred buy) and red (inferred sell) volume; the POC row is an amber outline. The buy/sell split is inferred, not measured order flow, and is computed only for this style.", display=display.none)
bool   vpMono         = inpVpStyle == "Monochrome"
bool   inpVpDelta     = not vpMono     // the buy/sell split is computed only when drawn
int    inpVpWidth     = input.int(14,     "        Width (bars)", minval=8, maxval=150, group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpNodes     = input.bool(false,  "        HVN / LVN marks", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpVa        = input.bool(true,  "    Value area (VAH / VAL)", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpPoc       = input.bool(true,  "    POC", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpTrail     = input.bool(false, "    Developing level trails", group=G_VP, tooltip="Off by default: three more lines following price, and the session's POC and value area are already drawn as levels.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpPrev      = input.bool(false,  "    Prior session levels", group=G_VP, tooltip="Last session's pPOC, pVAH and pVAL — three dotted lines, drawn only across the session in front of you. These are the reference the market is currently accepting or rejecting, which is why they are not stacked back through history.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpNaked     = input.bool(true,  "    Naked POCs", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
int    inpVpNakedMax  = input.int(3,      "        Max kept", minval=1, maxval=20, group=G_VP, tooltip="How many untouched POCs to keep. The oldest is dropped first.", display=display.none)
int    inpVpNakedAge  = input.int(250,    "        Max age (bars)", minval=50, maxval=1000, step=25, group=G_VP, tooltip="A naked POC older than this is dropped whether or not price ever traded through it, and no line starts further back than this. A point of control from four hundred bars ago describes a market that no longer exists.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpVwap      = input.bool(true,  "    Session VWAP", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpIb        = input.bool(true,  "    Initial balance (IBH / IBL)", group=G_VP, tooltip="Drawn on intraday charts only. On a daily chart the session is a week and the Initial Balance span outlasts it.", display=display.none)
int    inpVpIbBars    = input.int(12,     "        Span (bars)", minval=3, maxval=60, group=G_VP, display=display.none)

// ── gates, resolved once ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool   vpChartOn  = inpVpMaster
// THE MASTER NOW GATES COMPUTE AS WELL AS DRAWING. Before this it only silenced
// the chart objects while the accumulation loop, the row inserts and the value-
// area walk all still ran on every bar. A switch that turns the picture off and
// leaves the work on is not an off switch.
// the profile is built only when a layer drawn from it is on. VWAP and IB do not need it.
bool   vpCtxOn    = vpChartOn and (inpVpHistg or inpVpVa or inpVpPoc or inpVpTrail or inpVpPrev or inpVpNaked)
bool   vpIsIntra  = timeframe.isintraday
int    vpTfSec    = timeframe.in_seconds()
// AUTO-TPO FALLBACK. On a symbol reporting no volume every row received zero, so
// pocVol never exceeded zero and the `pocVol > 0` guard suppressed the histogram,
// the POC and the value area entirely - the profile simply did not appear, with
// nothing to explain why, and the panel still read "Volume" because it reported the
// user's INTENT rather than what happened. Index spot and most TVC symbols are
// exactly that case. The share of bars carrying real volume decides it now.
float  vpVolShare = ta.cum((na(volume) or volume == 0.0) ? 0.0 : 1.0) / (bar_index + 1)
bool   vpVolUsable= vpVolShare >= 0.5
bool   vpVolOff   = not inpVpUseVol or not vpVolUsable
bool   vpVolOk    = not vpVolOff          // what ACTUALLY happened, not what was asked
bool   vpTpoAuto  = inpVpUseVol and not vpVolUsable
string vpAnchorTf = vpIsIntra ? "D" : timeframe.isdaily ? "W" : "M"
// The first bar opens a session too. Without it the first partial session had no
// frozen bin width and no session start, so it drew no profile and its Initial
// Balance stretched across the whole of it. The flip is evaluated on its own line
// first so ta.change runs on every bar under v6's lazy `or`.
bool   vpSessFlip = ta.change(time(vpAnchorTf)) != 0
bool   vpNewSess  = barstate.isfirst or vpSessFlip
bool   vpHistOn   = vpChartOn and inpVpHistg and vpCtxOn
bool   vpVaOn     = vpChartOn and inpVpVa    and vpCtxOn
bool   vpPocOn    = vpChartOn and inpVpPoc   and vpCtxOn
bool   vpNodesOn  = vpHistOn  and inpVpNodes
bool   vpNakedOn  = vpChartOn and inpVpNaked and vpCtxOn
bool   vpPrevOn   = vpChartOn and inpVpPrev  and vpCtxOn
bool   vpTrailOn  = vpChartOn and inpVpTrail and vpCtxOn
bool   vpVwapOn   = vpChartOn and inpVpVwap
bool   vpIbOn     = vpChartOn and inpVpIb and vpIsIntra

// ATR floor. Floored to mintick so the session-start bin freeze never freezes to
// na and blanks the first session. ta.* must be evaluated on EVERY bar, never
// inside the session branch that consumes it.
float vpATR = math.max(nz(ta.atr(20), syminfo.mintick), syminfo.mintick)

// ── helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_vpLocate(array<int> keys, int k) =>
    int  lo    = 0
    int  hi    = array.size(keys) - 1
    int  pos   = 0
    bool found = false
    while lo <= hi
        int mid = (lo + hi) / 2
        int mk  = array.get(keys, mid)
        if mk == k
            pos   := mid
            found := true
            break
        else if mk < k
            lo := mid + 1
        else
            hi := mid - 1
    if not found
        pos := lo
    [pos, found]

f_vpAdd(array<int> keys, array<float> vols, array<float> buys, array<float> sells, int k, float v, float bv, float sv) =>
    [pos, found] = f_vpLocate(keys, k)
    float nv = v
    if found
        nv := array.get(vols, pos) + v
        array.set(vols,  pos, nv)
        array.set(buys,  pos, array.get(buys,  pos) + bv)
        array.set(sells, pos, array.get(sells, pos) + sv)
    else
        array.insert(keys,  pos, k)
        array.insert(vols,  pos, v)
        array.insert(buys,  pos, bv)
        array.insert(sells, pos, sv)
    nv

// ── profile state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var array<int>   vpKey  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> vpVol  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> vpBuy  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> vpSell = array.new<float>()
var float vpBin   = na
var float vpTotal = 0.0
var int   pocKey  = na
var float pocVol  = 0.0
var float poc     = na
var float vah     = na
var float vaLow   = na
var float prevPoc = na
var float prevVah = na
var float prevVal = na
var bool  vpIntraOk = false

// intrabar distribution (falls back automatically when unavailable)
// On a chart at or below one minute there is no lower timeframe worth spreading
// by, and on a SECONDS chart "1" is HIGHER than the chart - a runtime error. The
// request then asks for the chart's own timeframe (harmless) and intrabar
// distribution stands down.
string vpLtf      = vpTfSec >= 3600 ? "5" : vpTfSec > 60 ? "1" : timeframe.period
bool   vpIntraUse = inpVpIntrabar and vpTfSec > 60
[vpIbHi, vpIbLo, vpIbVol, vpIbClose] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, vpLtf, [high, low, volume, close])

// inferred delta (DISPLAY ONLY) — gap-aware close-location share to buyers
float vpTrHi  = math.max(high, nz(close[1], high))
float vpTrLo  = math.min(low,  nz(close[1], low))
float vpTrRng = math.max(vpTrHi - vpTrLo, syminfo.mintick)
float vpShare = inpVpDelta ? math.min(1.0, math.max(0.0, (close - vpTrLo) / vpTrRng)) : 0.5
float vpBarV  = vpVolOff ? 1.0 : math.max(nz(volume), 0.0)
float vpBarB  = vpBarV * vpShare
float vpBarS  = vpBarV - vpBarB

// The profile's accumulation and value-area walk, as a function: its loops
// sit outside the script's main body, whose length Pine caps. The four bin
// arrays are references; the state it changes comes back.
float vpC1 = close[1]
f_vpBuild(float tot0, int key0, float vol0, bool used0, float poc0, float vah0, float val0) =>
    float sTot  = tot0
    int   sKey  = key0
    float sVol  = vol0
    bool  sUsed = used0
    float sPoc  = poc0
    float sVah  = vah0
    float sVal  = val0
    if not na(vpBin) and vpBin > 0
        bool usedIntrabar = false
        if vpIntraUse and not na(vpIbHi) and not na(vpIbLo) and not na(vpIbVol) and not na(vpIbClose)
            int m = array.size(vpIbHi)
            if m > 0 and m == array.size(vpIbLo) and m == array.size(vpIbVol) and m == array.size(vpIbClose)
                usedIntrabar := true
                float prevC = vpC1
                for j = 0 to m - 1
                    float ih = array.get(vpIbHi, j)
                    float il = array.get(vpIbLo,  j)
                    // TPO: each CHART bar is one unit of time, split across its
                    // intrabars - otherwise an intrabar-built bar counted m times
                    // what a fallback bar counted in the same session.
                    float iv = vpVolOff ? 1.0 / m : math.max(nz(array.get(vpIbVol, j)), 0.0)
                    float ic = array.get(vpIbClose, j)
                    float bvn = iv * 0.5
                    float svn = iv * 0.5
                    if inpVpDelta and not na(ic) and not na(prevC)
                        if ic > prevC
                            bvn := iv
                            svn := 0.0
                        else if ic < prevC
                            bvn := 0.0
                            svn := iv
                    if not na(ic)
                        prevC := ic
                    if not na(ih) and not na(il)
                        int kl = int(math.floor(il / vpBin))
                        int kh = int(math.floor(ih / vpBin))
                        int nb = math.max(1, math.min(kh - kl + 1, 200))
                        float per  = iv  / nb
                        float perB = bvn / nb
                        float perS = svn / nb
                        for k = kl to kl + nb - 1
                            float tot = f_vpAdd(vpKey, vpVol, vpBuy, vpSell, k, per, perB, perS)
                            sTot += per
                            if tot > sVol
                                sVol := tot
                                sKey := k
        if not usedIntrabar
            int kl = int(math.floor(low  / vpBin))
            int kh = int(math.floor(high / vpBin))
            int nb = math.max(1, math.min(kh - kl + 1, 200))
            float per  = vpBarV / nb
            float perB = vpBarB / nb
            float perS = vpBarS / nb
            for k = kl to kl + nb - 1
                float tot = f_vpAdd(vpKey, vpVol, vpBuy, vpSell, k, per, perB, perS)
                sTot += per
                if tot > sVol
                    sVol := tot
                    sKey := k

        sUsed := usedIntrabar

    int nLev = array.size(vpKey)
    if nLev > 0 and not na(sKey) and not na(vpBin)
        [pi, pfound] = f_vpLocate(vpKey, sKey)
        if pfound
            float target = sTot * inpVpVaPct
            int   lo    = pi
            int   hi    = pi
            float acc   = array.get(vpVol, pi)
            int   guard = 0
            while acc < target and (lo > 0 or hi < nLev - 1) and guard < nLev + 2
                guard += 1
                float vd = lo > 0        ? array.get(vpVol, lo - 1) : -1.0
                float vu = hi < nLev - 1 ? array.get(vpVol, hi + 1) : -1.0
                if vu >= vd
                    hi  += 1
                    acc += vu
                else
                    lo  -= 1
                    acc += vd
            sPoc := (sKey + 0.5) * vpBin
            sVah := (array.get(vpKey, hi) + 1.0) * vpBin
            sVal := array.get(vpKey, lo) * vpBin
    [sTot, sKey, sVol, sUsed, sPoc, sVah, sVal]

if vpCtxOn
    if vpNewSess
        prevPoc := poc
        prevVah := vah
        prevVal := vaLow
        array.clear(vpKey)
        array.clear(vpVol)
        array.clear(vpBuy)
        array.clear(vpSell)
        vpTotal := 0.0
        pocKey  := na
        pocVol  := 0.0
        vpBin   := inpVpBinMode == "Fixed ticks" ? math.max(syminfo.mintick, inpVpBinTicks * syminfo.mintick) : math.max(syminfo.mintick, vpATR / inpVpBinsPerAtr)
    [bTot, bKey, bVol, bUsed, bPoc, bVah, bVal] = f_vpBuild(vpTotal, pocKey, pocVol, vpIntraOk, poc, vah, vaLow)
    vpTotal   := bTot
    pocKey    := bKey
    pocVol    := bVol
    vpIntraOk := bUsed
    poc       := bPoc
    vah       := bVah
    vaLow     := bVal

// ── naked POC ledger (measured) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//  Capped by input rather than at a hard twelve: twelve amber dotted lines on a
//  long chart stop being a reference and become the chart.
var array<float> vpNpY = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   vpNpX = array.new<int>()
if barstate.isconfirmed and array.size(vpNpY) > 0
    int kn = array.size(vpNpY) - 1
    while kn >= 0
        if high >= array.get(vpNpY, kn) and low <= array.get(vpNpY, kn)
            array.remove(vpNpY, kn)
            array.remove(vpNpX, kn)
        kn -= 1
if vpCtxOn and vpNewSess and not na(prevPoc)
    bool dupN = false
    if array.size(vpNpY) > 0
        for qn = 0 to array.size(vpNpY) - 1
            if math.abs(array.get(vpNpY, qn) - prevPoc) <= vpATR * 0.1
                dupN := true
                break
    if not dupN
        array.push(vpNpY, prevPoc)
        array.push(vpNpX, bar_index)
        while array.size(vpNpY) > inpVpNakedMax
            array.shift(vpNpY)
            array.shift(vpNpX)
while array.size(vpNpX) > 0
    if bar_index - array.get(vpNpX, 0) > inpVpNakedAge
        array.shift(vpNpY)
        array.shift(vpNpX)
    else
        break

// ── session VWAP + Initial Balance (measured) ─────────────────────────────────
var float vpSessPv = 0.0
var float vpSessVv = 0.0
var float vpIbh    = na
var float vpIbl    = na
var int   vpSessStart = na
if vpChartOn
    if vpNewSess
        vpSessPv    := 0.0
        vpSessVv    := 0.0
        vpIbh       := high
        vpIbl       := low
        vpSessStart := bar_index
    float wV = vpVolOff ? 1.0 : math.max(nz(volume), 1e-10)
    vpSessPv += hlc3 * wV
    vpSessVv += wV
    if bar_index - nz(vpSessStart, bar_index) < inpVpIbBars       // bars 0 … n-1 = n bars
        vpIbh := math.max(nz(vpIbh, high), high)
        vpIbl := math.min(nz(vpIbl, low), low)
float vpVwap = vpSessVv > 0 ? vpSessPv / vpSessVv : na

// ── right-edge tag column + collision control ─────────────────────────────────
int VP_GUTTER = 2
int VP_XBACK  = 5000          // furthest-back x any profile drawing may take
int VP_OFFSET = 0             // the +3 below already clears the node marks
int VP_CONE   = inpCone ? inpH : 0                          // the forward cone's bars: the profile sits to its right
int vpLeft    = bar_index + VP_CONE + 3 + VP_OFFSET
int vpRight   = vpLeft + inpVpWidth
var int tagX  = 0
var array<float> tagRows = array.new<float>()

f_rowFree(float y) =>
    float minGap = vpATR * 0.80                              // a tag is about this tall on a small chart
    bool  free   = true
    if array.size(tagRows) > 0
        for yy in tagRows
            if math.abs(yy - y) < minGap
                free := false
                break
    free

f_vpTag(label lb, float y, string txt, color col, bool on) =>
    label.delete(lb)
    bool draw = on and not na(y) and f_rowFree(y)
    if draw
        array.push(tagRows, y)
    draw ? label.new(tagX, y, txt + " " + str.tostring(y, format.mintick),
              xloc.bar_index, yloc.price, color.new(col, 88), label.style_label_left,
              col, size.tiny, force_overlay = true) : label(na)

// ── developing-level trails + VWAP curve (force_overlay) ──────────────────────
// Blank on the session-open bar so yesterday's finals never connect to today.
// force_overlay relocates these to the MAIN chart pane, so they render as price-
// level curves and never touch the pane's own scale.
plot(vpTrailOn and vpVaOn  and not vpNewSess ? vah   : na, "Profile · VAH trail", color.new(C_VA, 75), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plot(vpTrailOn and vpVaOn  and not vpNewSess ? vaLow : na, "Profile · VAL trail", color.new(C_VA, 75), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plot(vpTrailOn and vpPocOn and not vpNewSess ? poc   : na, "Profile · POC trail", color.new(C_POC, 65), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plot(vpVwapOn ? vpVwap : na, "Profile · VWAP", color.new(C_VWAP, 35), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)

// ── histogram (render aggregation into ≤110 rows) ─────────────────────────────
var array<box> vpBoxes = array.new<box>()
// Drawn by a function, out of the script's main body; it returns where the
// tag column starts.
f_vpRender() =>
    for b in vpBoxes
        box.delete(b)
    array.clear(vpBoxes)
    int tx = (vpHistOn ? vpRight : bar_index + VP_CONE) + VP_GUTTER
    if vpHistOn and not na(vpBin) and vpBin > 0 and pocVol > 0
        int maxRight = vpLeft
        int nB = array.size(vpKey)
        if nB > 0
            int ROWS_MAX = 110
            int step = math.max(1, int(math.ceil(nB / float(ROWS_MAX))))
            int nR   = int(math.ceil(nB / float(step)))
            array<float> rV  = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rB  = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rS  = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rLo = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rHi = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<bool>  rP  = array.new<bool>(nR, false)
            [pIdx, pFound] = f_vpLocate(vpKey, pocKey)
            for i = 0 to nB - 1
                int rr = int(math.floor(i / float(step)))
                array.set(rV, rr, array.get(rV, rr) + array.get(vpVol, i))
                array.set(rB, rr, array.get(rB, rr) + array.get(vpBuy, i))
                array.set(rS, rr, array.get(rS, rr) + array.get(vpSell, i))
                if i % step == 0
                    array.set(rLo, rr, array.get(vpKey, i) * vpBin)
                if i % step == step - 1 or i == nB - 1
                    array.set(rHi, rr, (array.get(vpKey, i) + 1.0) * vpBin)
                if pFound and i == pIdx
                    array.set(rP, rr, true)
            // Row width is normalised by the WIDEST RENDERED ROW, not by the raw
            // POC bin. Above ROWS_MAX bins the rows are aggregated in groups of
            // `step`, so an aggregated row holds several bins' worth and can
            // exceed pocVol — which made the histogram overshoot its declared
            // width by up to `step` times and drag the tag column off the screen
            // with it. Any session finer than 110 bins hit this.
            float rMax   = 0.0
            float hvMean = 0.0
            int   hvCnt  = 0
            for r0 = 0 to nR - 1
                float tv0 = array.get(rV, r0)
                rMax := math.max(rMax, tv0)
                if tv0 > 0
                    hvMean += tv0
                    hvCnt  += 1
            hvMean := hvCnt > 0 ? hvMean / hvCnt : 0.0
            float hvVar = 0.0
            for r0 = 0 to nR - 1
                float tv0 = array.get(rV, r0)
                if tv0 > 0
                    hvVar += math.pow(tv0 - hvMean, 2)
            float hvSd  = hvCnt > 0 ? math.sqrt(hvVar / hvCnt) : 0.0
            float hvnTh = hvMean + 1.2 * hvSd
            float lvnTh = hvMean - 0.6 * hvSd
            array<float> srtV = array.new<float>()
            for r0 = 0 to nR - 1
                if array.get(rV, r0) > 0
                    array.push(srtV, array.get(rV, r0))
            if array.size(srtV) > 10
                array.sort(srtV, order.ascending)
                lvnTh := array.get(srtV, math.max(0, int(math.floor(array.size(srtV) * 0.10))))
            for r = 0 to nR - 1
                if array.size(vpBoxes) >= 470
                    break
                float tV = array.get(rV, r)
                int wTot = tV > 0 and rMax > 0 ? int(math.round(inpVpWidth * tV / rMax)) : 0
                if wTot > 0
                    float yB    = array.get(rLo, r)
                    float ySpan = array.get(rHi, r) - yB
                    float yT    = yB + ySpan * 0.85
                    float pc    = yB + ySpan / 2.0
                    bool  isPoc = array.get(rP, r)
                    maxRight := math.max(maxRight, vpLeft + wTot)
                    bool inVa = not na(vah) and not na(vaLow) and pc >= vaLow and pc <= vah
                    int  fade = inVa ? 65 : 82                   // display only: quieter than the cone beside it
                    if vpMono
                        // MONOCHROME: one box per row, hue = identity never
                        // direction — amber POC row, blue value-area rows, grey
                        // out-of-value tails. POC row is a denser amber FILL.
                        color rowCol = isPoc ? C_POC : inVa ? C_VA : C_NODE
                        int   rowFd  = isPoc ? 45 : fade
                        array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft, yT, vpLeft + wTot, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(rowCol, rowFd), force_overlay = true))
                    else
                        // DELTA SPLIT: green inferred-buy / red inferred-sell, with
                        // the POC row marked by an amber OUTLINE so the split keeps
                        // its colour.
                        float bV = array.get(rB, r)
                        int   wB = tV > 0 ? int(math.round(wTot * bV / tV)) : 0
                        if wB > 0
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft, yT, vpLeft + wB, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_UP, fade), force_overlay = true))
                        if wTot - wB > 0
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft + wB, yT, vpLeft + wTot, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_DN, fade), force_overlay = true))
                        if isPoc
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft, yT, vpLeft + wTot, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(C_POC, 0), border_width = 1, bgcolor = na, force_overlay = true))
                    if vpNodesOn and r > 0 and r < nR - 1 and not isPoc and tV > 0
                        float vL = array.get(rV, r - 1)
                        float vR = array.get(rV, r + 1)
                        bool  peak   = tV > vL and tV > vR
                        bool  trough = tV < vL and tV < vR
                        // Node marks sit just LEFT of the histogram (vpLeft-2..vpLeft-1),
                        // so they travel with the profile's offset and keep a one-bar gap.
                        // HVN dense violet / LVN pale violet — disjoint from BOTH the
                        // monochrome grey tails and the delta-split green/red, so the
                        // colour reads in either style. Form still separates them:
                        // full-height block = node, centred tick = vacuum.
                        if tV >= hvnTh and peak
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft - 2, yT, vpLeft - 1, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_HVN, 40), force_overlay = true))
                        else if tV <= lvnTh and trough
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft - 2, pc - vpBin * 0.08, vpLeft - 1, pc + vpBin * 0.08, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_LVN, 40), force_overlay = true))
            if maxRight > vpLeft
                tx := maxRight + VP_GUTTER
    tx
if barstate.islast
    tagX := f_vpRender()

// ── right-edge tags and managed level lines · live tier, IB, prior session,
//    naked POCs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Rebuilt on the last bar by one function - out of the script's main body,
// whose length Pine caps - so every tag, line and box is kept in an array
// rather than a variable of its own. The live tags come first, as before, so
// the collision control seats them ahead of the prior session's.
var array<label> vpLvTags  = array.new<label>()
var array<line>  vpLvLines = array.new<line>()
var array<box>   vpLvBoxes = array.new<box>()
f_vpLevels() =>
    for lb in vpLvTags
        label.delete(lb)
    array.clear(vpLvTags)
    for ln in vpLvLines
        line.delete(ln)
    array.clear(vpLvLines)
    for bx in vpLvBoxes
        box.delete(bx)
    array.clear(vpLvBoxes)
    array.clear(tagRows)
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), poc,    "POC",  C_POC,    vpPocOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vah,    "VAH",  C_VA,     vpVaOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vaLow,  "VAL",  C_VA,     vpVaOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vpVwap, "VWAP", C_VWAP,   vpVwapOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vpIbh,  "IBH",  C_VIOLET, vpIbOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vpIbl,  "IBL",  C_VIOLET, vpIbOn))
    // Session-anchored. Pine refuses drawings placed more than 10,000 bars into
    // history; every x in this block is bounded by VP_XBACK well inside that. The
    // old bound of 400 cited max_bars_back, which does not govern drawings, and
    // cut session lines short on 24-hour 1-minute charts (1,440 bars a session).
    int xSess = math.max(math.max(not na(vpSessStart) ? vpSessStart : 0, bar_index - VP_XBACK), 0)
    if vpPocOn and not na(poc)
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, poc, bar_index, poc, color = color.new(C_POC, 20), width = 1, force_overlay = true))
    if vpVaOn and not na(vah) and not na(vaLow)
        array.push(vpLvBoxes, box.new(xSess, vah, bar_index, vaLow, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_VA, 95), force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vah,   bar_index, vah,   color = color.new(C_VA, 50), width = 1, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vaLow, bar_index, vaLow, color = color.new(C_VA, 50), width = 1, force_overlay = true))
    if vpIbOn and not na(vpIbh)
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vpIbh, bar_index, vpIbh, color = color.new(C_VIOLET, 60), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vpIbl, bar_index, vpIbl, color = color.new(C_VIOLET, 60), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true))
    if vpPrevOn and not na(prevPoc)
        int xA = xSess                                            // across the session in front of you, as the tooltip says
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xA, prevPoc, bar_index, prevPoc, color = color.new(C_POC, 55), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xA, prevVah, bar_index, prevVah, color = color.new(C_VA, 55),  width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xA, prevVal, bar_index, prevVal, color = color.new(C_VA, 55),  width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), prevPoc, "pPOC", C_POC, vpPrevOn))
        array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), prevVah, "pVAH", C_VA,  vpPrevOn))
        array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), prevVal, "pVAL", C_VA,  vpPrevOn))
    if vpNakedOn and array.size(vpNpY) > 0
        int xMinN = math.max(0, bar_index - math.min(inpVpNakedAge, VP_XBACK))
        int nN    = array.size(vpNpY)
        for i = 0 to nN - 1
            float ny = array.get(vpNpY, i)
            int   x1 = math.max(xMinN, array.get(vpNpX, i))
            if not (vpPrevOn and ny == prevPoc)                       // the newest naked POC is the prior session's: not drawn twice
                array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(x1, ny, bar_index, ny, color = color.new(C_POC, 55), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
if barstate.islast
    f_vpLevels()

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  8 · THE PANE
//
//  The columns are the surprise, clipped at ±4 for display so the tapes keep
//  their place; the two lines are the learned bands it is judged against.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
bool vSur = inpPane == "Surprise"
bool vPrf = inpPane == "Proof"

// GEOMETRY. Columns and band are clipped at ±CLIP so the tapes keep their place
// and nothing can stretch the scale. Inner tapes are full height; the outer,
// context-only tapes are about half.
const float CLIP   = 3.5
const float TAPE_Y = 4.3                                    // inner tapes: 3.90 - 4.70
const float TAPE_H = 0.40
const float OUT_Y  = 5.15                                   // outer tapes: 4.93 - 5.37
const float OUT_H  = 0.22

// COLUMNS. Two channels, one meaning each:
//   OPACITY  the measured event - solid when the close left the landing band,
//            faint inside it;
//   HUE      description - green up / red down when the trend backs the move,
//            neutral when it does not. A miss the trend does not back is drawn
//            in the brightest neutral, never in the grey that means "nothing".
bool  cWith = (u >= 0.0 and trRaw == 2) or (u < 0.0 and trRaw == 0)
color cHue  = cWith ? (u >= 0.0 ? C_UP : C_DN) : C_NEUT
color cCol  = not settled ? color.new(C_NEUT, 86) : mU or mD ? color.new(cWith ? cHue : C_TEXT, 0) : color.new(cHue, cWith ? 62 : 76)
plot(vSur ? math.max(-CLIP, math.min(CLIP, u)) : na,       "Surprise · columns (σ, clipped)", cCol, 1, plot.style_columns, display = display.pane, precision = 2)
plot(u,                                                    "Surprise (σ)",                    cCol, 1, display = display.status_line + display.data_window, precision = 2)
plot(vSur and not na(bU) ? math.min(bU, CLIP)   : na,      "Landing band · upper (σ)",        color.new(C_CONE, 20), 1, display = display.pane + display.data_window, precision = 2)
plot(vSur and not na(bD) ? math.max(-bD, -CLIP) : na,      "Landing band · lower (σ)",        color.new(C_CONE, 20), 1, display = display.pane + display.data_window, precision = 2)
hline(0.0, "Zero", color.new(C_NEUT, 70), hline.style_dotted)

plot(vPrf and nP > 0 ? 100.0 * math.log(eqF) : na, "Proof · exposure (log %)",     color.new(C_CONE, 0),  2, display = display.pane + display.data_window, precision = 1)
plot(vPrf and nP > 0 ? 100.0 * math.log(eqH) : na, "Proof · buy and hold (log %)", color.new(C_NEUT, 20), 1, display = display.pane + display.data_window, precision = 1)

// ── the tapes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INNER pair - what the cone and exposure read - may reach full strength.
// OUTER pair - context - is thinner and never does. A tape with no reading
// yet is neutral grey.
bool tapesOn = vSur and inpTapes

// TREND · hue is the side, in the DEEP tone of the long horizon; faint while
// flat, a step at ±0.5σ, solid by 1.5σ.
float tAbs  = math.abs(T)
color tHue  = T >= 0.0 ? C_UPD : C_DND                      // deep: the long horizon
color tInk  = T >= 0.0 ? C_UP : C_DN                        // the same side, bright, for text
color tapeT = na(T) ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : tAbs < 0.5 ? color.from_gradient(tAbs, 0.0, 0.5, color.new(tHue, 90), color.new(tHue, 62)) :
     color.from_gradient(tAbs, 0.5, 1.5, color.new(tHue, 40), color.new(tHue, 0))

// STRETCH LADDER (outer) · hue is the side it leans; strength is how many rungs
// are outside their own band on that side. Capped: it carries no direction.
color lHue  = ladX >= 0.0 ? C_UP : C_DN
color tapeL = not ladOk ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : ladN >= 3 ? color.new(lHue, 35) : ladN >= 1 ? color.new(lHue, 65) :
     color.from_gradient(math.abs(ladX), 0.0, 1.0, color.new(lHue, 94), color.new(lHue, 82))

// RISK · gold only: next to nothing while calm, a step at normal, a step at
// stressed, solid toward the top of its range.
color tapeR = not regOk ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : regRaw == 2 ? color.from_gradient(prk, 200.0 / 3.0, 100.0, color.new(C_GOLD, 40), color.new(C_GOLD, 0)) :
     regRaw == 1 ? color.from_gradient(prk, 100.0 / 3.0, 200.0 / 3.0, color.new(C_GOLD, 80), color.new(C_GOLD, 62)) : color.from_gradient(prk, 0.0, 100.0 / 3.0, color.new(C_GOLD, 95), color.new(C_GOLD, 86))

// RISK MOMENTUM (outer) · gold while risk is rising, capped below the risk
// tape's own gold; grey while it is falling; faint steady.
float rmAbs = math.abs(rMom)
color tapeM = na(rMom) ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : rmS == 2 ? color.from_gradient(rmAbs, 0.10, 0.40, color.new(C_GOLD, 60), color.new(C_GOLD, 30)) :
     rmS == 0 ? color.from_gradient(rmAbs, 0.10, 0.40, color.new(C_NEUT, 78), color.new(C_NEUT, 60)) : color.new(C_NEUT, 92)

plot(tapesOn ?  TAPE_Y + TAPE_H : na, "Tape · trend",          tapeT, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase =  TAPE_Y - TAPE_H, display = display.pane)
plot(tapesOn ?  OUT_Y  + OUT_H  : na, "Tape · stretch ladder", tapeL, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase =  OUT_Y  - OUT_H,  display = display.pane)
plot(tapesOn ? -TAPE_Y + TAPE_H : na, "Tape · risk",           tapeR, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase = -TAPE_Y - TAPE_H, display = display.pane)
plot(tapesOn ? -OUT_Y  + OUT_H  : na, "Tape · risk momentum",  tapeM, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase = -OUT_Y  - OUT_H,  display = display.pane)

// What each tape says, in words - long for tooltips, short for labels and the
// table. One word for "not ready": warming.
string trTxt  = na(T) ? "warming" : (trRaw == 2 ? "up " : trRaw == 0 ? "down " : "flat ") + f_num(T, "+0.0;-0.0") + "σ"
string ladTxt = not ladOk ? "warming" : ladUp == 0 and ladDn == 0 ? "all four rungs inside" :
     (ladUp > 0 ? str.tostring(ladUp) + " of 4 above" : "") + (ladUp > 0 and ladDn > 0 ? " · " : "") + (ladDn > 0 ? str.tostring(ladDn) + " of 4 below" : "")
string regTxt = not regOk ? "warming" : regRaw == 0 ? "calm" : regRaw == 2 ? "stressed" : "normal"
string trWord   = na(T) ? "warming" : trRaw == 2 ? "up" : trRaw == 0 ? "down" : "flat"
string ladShort = not ladOk ? "warming" : ladUp == 0 and ladDn == 0 ? "inside" : (ladUp > 0 ? str.tostring(ladUp) + " above" : "") + (ladUp > 0 and ladDn > 0 ? " " : "") + (ladDn > 0 ? str.tostring(ladDn) + " below" : "")
string rmWord   = na(rMom) ? "warming" : rmS == 2 ? "rising" : rmS == 0 ? "falling" : "steady"

// ── on the price chart ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Three lines follow price, all in the cone's blue and all one pixel: the
// midline, quiet; the landing band's two edges, quieter. None reaches the
// status line or the price scale.
plot(inpLand ? upper[inpH] : na,  "Landing band · upper",   color.new(C_CONE, 78), 1, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plot(inpLand ? lower[inpH] : na,  "Landing band · lower",   color.new(C_CONE, 78), 1, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plot(inpTrail ? stopL : na,       "Stop history · long",    color.new(C_DN, 70), 1, plot.style_stepline, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plot(inpTrail ? stopS : na,       "Stop history · short",   color.new(C_UP, 70), 1, plot.style_stepline, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plot(inpMid ? midL : na,          "Midline",                color.new(C_CONE, 55), 1, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.data_window)
plotshape(inpMid and inpMidMk and midUp and barstate.isconfirmed, "Midline · close above", shape.circle, location.belowbar, color.new(C_UP, 45), size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane)
plotshape(inpMid and inpMidMk and midDn and barstate.isconfirmed, "Midline · close below", shape.circle, location.abovebar, color.new(C_DN, 45), size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane)
plotshape(inpMark and provenUp,   "Proven state · positive", shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.new(C_UP, 45), size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane)
plotshape(inpMark and provenDn,   "Proven state · negative", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(C_DN, 45), size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane)

// The cone and stops are drawings, and drawings do not move the price scale.
// Two invisible points on the last bar keep both stops on screen.
float topY = math.max(stopS, upper)
float botY = math.min(stopL, lower)
plot(inpCone and coneOk ? topY : na, "Scale anchor · top",    color.new(C_CONE, 100), 1, show_last = 1, editable = false, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane)
plot(inpCone and coneOk ? botY : na, "Scale anchor · bottom", color.new(C_CONE, 100), 1, show_last = 1, editable = false, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane)

// ── the forward cone, the stops, and the tapes' names ─────────────────────
// The loudest thing on the chart: the cone at two pixels and the stops solid.
// Each stop is named on itself - the short stop above the cone's far corner,
// the long stop below it - clear of the cone's outline and of the profile.
var polyline plCone = na
var line     lnL    = na
var line     lnS    = na
var array<label> lbs = array.new<label>()

f_stopTag(float py, string txt, color c, bool above) =>
    label.new(bar_index + inpH, py, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(c, 100),
         style = above ? label.style_label_lower_right : label.style_label_upper_right, textcolor = c, size = size.small, force_overlay = true)
f_tapeTag(float py, string txt, color c) =>
    label.new(bar_index + 1, py, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(c, 100), style = label.style_label_left,
         textcolor = c, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_left)

if barstate.islast
    polyline.delete(plCone)
    line.delete(lnL)
    line.delete(lnS)
    while array.size(lbs) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(lbs))
    if inpCone and coneOk
        array<chart.point> pts = array.new<chart.point>()
        for i = 0 to inpH
            array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(bar_index + i, close * math.exp(qU * sig * math.sqrt(i))))
        for i = inpH to 0
            array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(bar_index + i, close * math.exp(-qD * sig * math.sqrt(i))))
        plCone := polyline.new(pts, curved = false, closed = true, xloc = xloc.bar_index, line_color = color.new(C_CONE, 0),
             fill_color = color.new(C_CONE, 84), line_width = 2, force_overlay = true)
        lnL := line.new(bar_index, stopL, bar_index + inpH, stopL, color = color.new(C_DN, 0), width = 2, style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true)
        lnS := line.new(bar_index, stopS, bar_index + inpH, stopS, color = color.new(C_UP, 0), width = 2, style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true)
        array.push(lbs, f_stopTag(topY, "SHORT STOP " + f_px(stopS), C_UP, true))
        array.push(lbs, f_stopTag(botY, "LONG STOP " + f_px(stopL), C_DN, false))
    if tapesOn
        array.push(lbs, f_tapeTag( (TAPE_Y + OUT_Y) / 2.0, "LADDER " + ladShort + "\nTREND " + trWord, na(T) ? C_NEUT : tInk))
        array.push(lbs, f_tapeTag(-(TAPE_Y + OUT_Y) / 2.0, "RISK " + regTxt + "\nMOMENTUM " + rmWord, regRaw == 2 or rmS == 2 ? C_GOLD : C_NEUT))

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  9 · THE TABLE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_stName(int s) =>
    string a = s < 3 ? "trend down" : s < 6 ? "trend flat" : "trend up"
    string b = s % 3 == 0 ? "closed below the band" : s % 3 == 2 ? "closed above the band" : "inside the band"
    a + " · " + b

f_cell(table t, int rw, string k, string val, color c, string tip) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, rw, k,   text_color = C_NEUT, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left,  tooltip = tip)
    table.cell(t, 1, rw, val, text_color = c,      text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right, tooltip = tip)

// Eight rows, in order of how much evidence stands behind them: the cone and
// stops, exposure, this chart's record of them, then context, then the proof.
// Every value names its own units, so it reads without the tooltip.
var table tb = na
if inpTbl and barstate.islast
    if na(tb)
        tb := table.new(inpPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right : inpPos == "Bottom right" ? position.bottom_right :
             inpPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left : position.bottom_left, 2, 8, bgcolor = C_PANEL,
             frame_color = color.new(C_NEUT, 75), frame_width = 1, border_width = 0, force_overlay = true)
    string hTxt = str.tostring(inpH) + " bars"
    if na(sig)
        f_cell(tb, 0, "PRAGYAM", "warming " + str.tostring(bar_index + 1) + "/" + str.tostring(WARM + inpH), C_NEUT,
             "The risk forecast needs a year of bars before its first reading.")
    else
        float dL  = 1.0 - stopL / close
        float dS  = stopS / close - 1.0
        float cov = nF > 0 ? 1.0 - (nMU + nMD) / nF : na
        f_cell(tb, 0, "CONE " + str.tostring(inpCover, "#") + "%", f_px(lower) + " – " + f_px(upper), C_CONE,
             "Where the close should be " + hTxt + " from now, this share of the time.")
        f_cell(tb, 1, "LONG STOP", f_px(stopL) + " · size " + f_pct(inpRisk / 100.0 / dL, "#"), ladOk and ladDn >= 3 ? C_GOLD : C_DN,
             "Touched within " + hTxt + " " + str.tostring(inpStop, "#") + "% of the time. Size: the position, as a share of equity, that loses " + str.tostring(inpRisk) + "% of equity there. Gold: three or four ladder rungs are below their bands - there it is touched about a quarter of the time.")
        f_cell(tb, 2, "SHORT STOP", f_px(stopS) + " · size " + f_pct(inpRisk / 100.0 / dS, "#"), C_UP,
             "Touched within " + hTxt + " " + str.tostring(inpStop, "#") + "% of the time, and the position size that goes with it.")
        f_cell(tb, 3, "EXPOSURE", f_pct(E, "#"), C_TEXT,
             "The share of a full position to carry: " + f_pct(dial, "#") + " = risk " + f_pct(dialR, "#") + (inpMode == "Risk only" ? "" : " × trend " + f_pct(dialT, "#")) + ", changed in steps. Daily and weekly charts only: on hourly bars it lost to buy and hold.")
        f_cell(tb, 4, "RECORD", "cone " + f_pct(cov, "#") + " · stops " + f_num(nF > 0 ? 100.0 * nMS / nF : na, "#") + "/" + f_pct(nF > 0 ? nMR / nF : na, "#"), math.abs(cov - inpCover / 100.0) > 0.03 ? C_GOLD : C_TEXT,
             "This chart's own record over " + str.tostring(nF) + " forecasts: how often the cone held (target " + str.tostring(inpCover, "#") + "%; last 250: " + f_pct(covRecent, "#") + ") and how often the long / short stop was touched (target " + str.tostring(inpStop, "#") + "%). Gold when the cone is more than 3 points off.")
        f_cell(tb, 5, "RISK", "±" + f_pct(sH, "#.0") + " · " + regTxt + (rmS == 1 or na(rMom) ? "" : " · " + rmWord), regRaw == 2 or rmS == 2 ? C_GOLD : C_TEXT,
             "One standard move over " + hTxt + " (" + f_pct(sig * math.sqrt(bpy), "#") + " a year); where risk stands in its last 500 bars; and whether it rose or fell more than 10% over " + hTxt + ". A rise usually fades.")
        f_cell(tb, 6, "TREND", trWord + " · ladder " + ladShort, na(T) ? C_NEUT : tInk,
             "Trend " + trTxt + ". Ladder: " + ladTxt + " (" + str.tostring(h0) + ", " + str.tostring(inpH) + ", " + str.tostring(h2) + ", " + str.tostring(h3) + " bars). " +
             (st < 0 ? "" : "State: " + f_stName(st) + " - " + (na(lZ) ? "too few on this chart to judge." : "seen " + f_num(lNe, "#") + " times, next " + hTxt + " " + f_num(lMu, "+0.00;-0.00") + "σ against " + f_num(gM, "+0.00;-0.00") + "σ usual: " + (proven == 1 ? "proven positive." : proven == -1 ? "proven negative." : "unproven."))))
        f_cell(tb, 7, "SHARPE", f_num(shF, "0.00") + " · B&H " + f_num(shH, "0.00"), C_TEXT,
             "Following exposure against buy and hold (B&H) on this chart, one bar late, net of costs. Worst drawdown " + f_pct(ddF, "#") + " against " + f_pct(ddH, "#") + "." +
             (inpMid ? " Midline rule (long above, flat below): Sharpe " + f_num(shM, "0.00") + "; " + str.tostring(mRuns) + " runs, " + f_pct(mRuns > 0 ? mWon / mRuns : na, "#") + " won, " + f_pct(mRuns > 0 ? mLong / mRuns : na, "#") + " lasted 20+ bars." : ""))

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ALERTS
//
//  Title: object · event. Message: symbol and timeframe, what happened, one
//  consequence. None of them is a trade signal, and the wording says so.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
alertcondition(mU and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Landing band · close above",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · closed above the landing band. A miss, not a signal.")
alertcondition(mD and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Landing band · close below",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · closed below the landing band. A miss, not a signal.")
alertcondition(ladOk and ladUp >= 3 and not (ladUp[1] >= 3) and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Stretch ladder · 3+ rungs above",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · 3 or 4 ladder rungs closed above their bands. No measured direction.")
alertcondition(ladOk and ladDn >= 3 and not (ladDn[1] >= 3) and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Stretch ladder · 3+ rungs below",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · 3 or 4 ladder rungs closed below their bands. Long stops are touched more often than stated here.")
alertcondition(regRaw == 2 and regRaw[1] != 2 and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Risk · stressed",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · risk entered the top third of its last 500 bars. Cone and stops widen; exposure falls.")
alertcondition(rmS == 2 and rmS[1] != 2 and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Risk · rising",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · risk rose more than 10% in one horizon. Such rises usually fade.")
alertcondition(midUp and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Midline · close above",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · closed above the midline. Not a signal.")
alertcondition(midDn and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Midline · close below",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · closed below the midline. Not a signal.")
alertcondition(E != E[1] and not na(E[1]) and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Exposure · changed",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · exposure moved one step. See the table's EXPOSURE row.")
alertcondition(provenUp, title = "Ledger · proven state, positive",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · entered a state this chart's history has proven positive. This chart's own record only.")
alertcondition(provenDn, title = "Ledger · proven state, negative",
     message = "{{ticker}} {{interval}} · entered a state this chart's history has proven negative. This chart's own record only.")
